{"id": "EUVD-2026-86814", "enisaUuid": "5653e122-0223-33ed-a14a-19f9d5d83bde", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nperf/x86/intel: Prevent drain_pebs() reentry\n\nThe PEBS buffer is shared by all events on a CPU, so drain_pebs() must\nnot be reentered. If so, one instance may observe stale buffer state and\npotentially access out-of-bound memory.\n\nMost invocations happen in NMI context, which naturally prevents reentry.\nHowever, drain_pebs() is also reachable from process context via\nintel_pmu_drain_pebs_buffer().\n\nIn those paths, the PMU is often already disabled, but not guaranteed.\nFor example, __intel_pmu_pebs_disable() only disables the target counter,\nso other active counters can still raise a PMI and interrupt an in-flight\ndrain_pebs(). Here is an example,\n\n__perf_addr_filters_adjust()\n  perf_event_stop()\n    __perf_event_stop()\n      x86_pmu_stop() (event->pmu->stop)\n        intel_pmu_disable_event()\n          intel_pmu_pebs_disable()\n            __intel_pmu_pebs_disable()\n              intel_pmu_drain_large_pebs()\n                intel_pmu_drain_pebs_buffer()\n\nIntroduce __intel_pmu_quiesce() and __intel_pmu_resume() helpers and\nuse them in intel_pmu_drain_large_pebs() to disable the full PMU\naround the intel_pmu_drain_pebs_buffer() call, preventing reentry.\n\nAlso add a warning in intel_pmu_drain_pebs_buffer() when the full PMU is\nnot disabled.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9882068ed242fcd4743f53027e8c790e88dcafff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/999e482fdf89400cc1ae937680fc05096b4c915b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5fe19dd8b3ed5fad6e5e0f0c58c7245043ee4af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c55599c0ec2aa020e41a0599c3044c56d8a2e7d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a56c03a397e2cd0c4cf8da96dcd6214f7d0e7d8c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5xpp-w3qp-6w34", "CVE-2026-97960"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07c76250-75f4-3ff0-8f56-4e180d3a3208", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b752ea0c28e3f7f0aaaad6abf84f735eebc37a60 <a56c03a397e2cd0c4cf8da96dcd6214f7d0e7d8c"}, {"id": "1481f2e4-ea6b-3cc4-bc4a-7506b9b8f215", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3.7 <6.4"}, {"id": "1e1f0b5c-87de-3c9d-a3f9-bea418e8f3d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "23426b13-19f0-34bd-801e-95c7e5ff771c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9165207b2b07415eeb01b3ac8bb84976ec96984"}, {"id": "3dc780d2-4099-311f-9d01-7d23adb40619", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "4c675507-c4cc-359b-8527-f7af0901fdce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b752ea0c28e3f7f0aaaad6abf84f735eebc37a60 <9882068ed242fcd4743f53027e8c790e88dcafff"}, {"id": "863fad2c-28f9-3727-815a-c715a67e8548", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b752ea0c28e3f7f0aaaad6abf84f735eebc37a60 <c55599c0ec2aa020e41a0599c3044c56d8a2e7d9"}, {"id": "b37dab19-0f0c-3195-bd75-b4411f80cf67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b8f6fc90-df49-3b65-86b8-fdf19db152b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b752ea0c28e3f7f0aaaad6abf84f735eebc37a60 <999e482fdf89400cc1ae937680fc05096b4c915b"}, {"id": "d2e20579-57a4-34f8-b182-31bfcafc7f08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "d455b79e-7040-3c47-8138-e2b43c7f7cdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b752ea0c28e3f7f0aaaad6abf84f735eebc37a60 <a5fe19dd8b3ed5fad6e5e0f0c58c7245043ee4af"}, {"id": "ea7cf60